---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import RiskCard from '../components/RiskCard.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config.mjs';
import { hazards, multipliers, risks, maturityCounts } from '../lib/data.mjs';

const count = (level) => maturityCounts.find((m) => m.level === level)?.n ?? 0;
const heroImage = null; // {{hero-image}}: to be decided. While empty, the hero is text only.
const words = ['no', 'one', 'two', 'three', 'four', 'five', 'six', 'seven', 'eight', 'nine', 'ten', 'eleven', 'twelve', 'thirteen', 'fourteen', 'fifteen', 'sixteen', 'seventeen'];
const w = (n) => words[n] ?? String(n);
---
<Base newsletter>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class={`hero-grid${heroImage ? ' has-visual' : ''}`}>
        <div class="text">
          <h1>{site.name}</h1>
          <p class="lead">{site.description}</p>
          <p>The Monitor describes {hazards.length} risks that could cause a global catastrophe this century, and {w(multipliers.length)} conditions that make them worse. For each one it lists the institutions and treaties that exist to reduce the risk and rates how mature that governance is. Of these {risks.length} entries, {count('Fully developed') === 0 ? 'none has' : `${w(count('Fully developed'))} have`} fully developed governance: {w(count('Developed'))} are rated Developed, {w(count('Developing'))} Developing and {w(count('Nascent'))} Nascent.</p>
          <div class="btn-row">
            <a class="btn" href="/about/">About the Monitor</a>
            <a class="btn" href="/risks/">Browse all risks</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        {heroImage && <div class="visual"><img src={heroImage} alt="" /></div>}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="risks">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Explore the risks</h2>
      <p class="measure" style="margin-top:0.5em">Each card is one risk. It shows how likely the risk is to reach catastrophic scale by 2100 and how mature its multilateral governance is. The colour shows the domain.</p>
      <div class="cards">
        {hazards.map((r) => <RiskCard risk={r} />)}
        <a class="card card-cta" href="/risks/">
          <h3>Looking for a specific risk?</h3>
          <span class="go">Browse and filter all risks →</span>
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="multiplier-block">
        <h3>Risk multipliers</h3>
        <p>{w(multipliers.length).replace(/^./, (c) => c.toUpperCase())} conditions that raise the likelihood or severity of every risk. They are not placed on the likelihood and impact scales.</p>
        <div class="cards">
          {multipliers.map((r) => <RiskCard risk={r} />)}
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="info-cards">
        <div class="info-card">
          <h3>How to read the Monitor</h3>
          <p>How the risks were selected, how likelihood and impact are assessed, and how the maturity of governance is scored on four pillars.</p>
          <a class="btn" href="/method/">Read the method</a>
        </div>
        <div class="info-card">
          <h3>Why a Monitor?</h3>
          <p>The UN Pact for the Future commits states to address global catastrophic and existential risks. The Monitor tracks how far the institutions have come.</p>
          <a class="btn" href="/about/">Learn more</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
